{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex","id":863625,"title":"Technocracy and Pentex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-11T07:26:51-07:00","id":863625,"title":"Technocracy and Pentex","content":"Why Technocracy have not crushed Pentex, even after Dimensional Anomaly? I bet Syndicate alone could utterly dismantle and obliterate Pentex like child's play if they desire so. I'm very curious about cause of their inaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-11-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:30:59-07:00","id":863627,"title":"","content":"They don't quite know. As far as the Convention Book tells it. They know that SPD is simply gone, but the funds keep coming in. They don't know anything more about it and try to cover the whole thing up, lest the Union blows. (The new Convention Books all offer the plot line that a technocratic civil war is imminent.)<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want the Syndicate to rip Pentex to pieces in your game that is certainly fine. They made have some interesting problem cleaning up afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11524-the_1of3","name":"The_1of3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:37:27-07:00","id":863631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_1of3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=863627#post863627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't quite know. As far as the Convention Book tells it. They know that SPD is simply gone, but the funds keep coming in. They don't know anything more about it and try to cover the whole thing up, lest the Union blows. (The new Convention Books all offer the plot line that a technocratic civil war is imminent.)<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want the Syndicate to rip Pentex to pieces in your game that is certainly fine. They made have some interesting problem cleaning up afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. And it is directly contradicted with contents of 2014 Book of the Wyrm. In the Book of the Wyrm, Syndicate certainly knows SPD's involvement with Pentex and has done nothing significant yet.<br /> 2. What problem exactly do you suggest? Could you more elaborate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:06:21-07:00","id":863656,"title":"","content":"The Project twilight book suggests, that the technocracy knows a bit about the omega plan and is moving to interdict it Though, to be fair, its an old book and omega plan isnt even MENTIONED in W20 book of the wyrm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-11-2016, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:49:34-07:00","id":863723,"title":"","content":"The basic reason they don't is that Pentex is a major global actor that they can't destroy without calling <i>significant</i> attention to their own dealings - made willingly and knowingly - with a force that is, at its core, inherently opposed to the end goals of the Technocracy. They have over 134 offices worldwide, possess major market shares in pharmaceuticals, weapons manufacturing, private military companies, waste disposal, mining, energy generation, oil extraction and refining, food processing, logistics and distribution, mass market media shares, fishery operations, cosmetics, raw plastics and paper production, tobacco products, global stocks and real-estate investment, and healthcare. Through Tellus and Sunburst, they have major shares of the computing world. Nastrum brings a major market share in the aerospace and military sector. Their sticky fingers even go into education and childcare.<br /> <br /> Endron alone has seven nuclear plants in America with 5 more slated to be built as of 2000 - and if on schedule, now built and operational. They control the most important oil pipeline in the entire Middle East, the Aswan-61 pipeline. Magadon has over 60 production plants and a dozen research plants worldwide, and a <i>22.5%</i> market share in 1998. In 1999 they made 24.8 billion dollars gross, and in 2000, posted a net profit of <i>8.115 billion</i>. O'Tolley's has a 25+% market share in the CONUS - for reference, <i>McDonalds</i>, that veritable juggernaut of Greasy Meat-Based Capitalism, only has a <i>19%</i> market share IRL. In 2010, an Endron rig spilled <i>250 million gallons of oil</i> - and that barely put a dent in the company's pockets. Deepwater Horizon was 210 million.<br /> <br /> That's why the Syndicate and the Technocracy doesn't 'crush' Pentex. You don't crush Pentex without also crushing the entire Western economy with it. It isn't some pesky little tick the Technocracy can pull out - it's a tapeworm wound so deep through the entire Western economic model that if you try and brute force it out, you're going to quickly find yourself elbow-deep in blood wondering why everything is screaming. Not only would the Syndicate taking the action expose them to massive problems with the rest of the Technocracy, the Technocracy simply <i>can't</i> crush Pentex without prolonged, difficult struggle. And before anyone goes 'well they're magic!', the global financial recession happened when the Syndicate got too 'experimental' - and Pentex have their own nephandi to call on.<br /> <br /> Pentex is the ugliest side of the concept of the corporation magnified to an extreme. It doesn't just 'go away'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:35:00-07:00","id":863793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=863631#post863631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. And it is directly contradicted with contents of 2014 Book of the Wyrm. In the Book of the Wyrm, Syndicate certainly knows SPD's involvement with Pentex and has done nothing significant yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of by design. The Convention Books are in line with the Revised metaplot, albeit in a timeline where Ascension never happened, and the Red Star faded. W20 BotW is very roughly setting neutral, existing somewhere between the Second Edition and Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:22:15-07:00","id":864045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=863723#post863723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And before anyone goes 'well they're magic!', the global financial recession happened when the Syndicate got too 'experimental' - and Pentex have their own nephandi to call on.<br /> <br /> Pentex is the ugliest side of the concept of the corporation magnified to an extreme. It doesn't just 'go away'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that they'd need to call on Nephandi to deal with recessions. They'd just cut corners and frighten out tax breaks and other concessions with dire warnings of woe vaguely hinting at how bad high unemployment would look. Fallen mages are more something that they'd contract to deal with spirits and various other types of otherworldly phenomena, and they can't contract a BSD Theurge, say because they don't want the tribe to know about a particular deal that they're brokering because it would put them at odds with the company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T19:32:48-07:00","id":864048,"title":"","content":"Oh, I didn't mean to deal with recessions - I meant to fight fire with fire if the Technocracy brought down its full weight to try and magically erase Pentex. The recessions, Chernobyl-scale nuclear disasters, and mass-poisonings would all be purely mundane consequences of trying to pluck Pentex from the face of the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T22:57:05-07:00","id":864134,"title":"","content":"If Pentex is <i>that </i>powerful, exactly how they have managed to grow into their current bloated monstrosity without help of true magic or genius? You are basically asserting Pentex has become <i>somehow </i>bigger, wealthier, economically more powerful than paradigm-shaking-and-defining Syndicate magic men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-12-2016, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:20:17-07:00","id":864143,"title":"","content":"They have the help of true magic, the help of spiritual entities, the help of hedge mages, and most terrifyingly of all: they have the help of very good lawyers. That Pentex is so vast isn't actually unbelievable - it's exaggerated, but it's in the same league as real-life 'megacorporations' like Berkshire Hathaway, ExxonMobil, General Electric or Morgan Chase. Companies already become unimaginably vast and powerful without recourse to magic IRL - why should they not do the same in the World of Darkness? Nestle, PepsiCo and Kraft together more or less completely control the processed food game, and actively influence global geopolitics and economic policy of entire nations. The largest publicly traded company in the world, ICBC, has assets equal to a full 30th of the world's total GDP and a GDP greater than all but the top three GDPs in the entire world. Corporations already grow into monstrosities without the aid of true magic. True magic and literal deals-with-the-devil just make it easier.<br /> <br /> Additionally, you don't have to be bigger than the Syndicate to pose a problem. All you have to do is comprise a <i>significant</i> portion of the world's total trade to make it unfeasible to simply eradicate you in a single fell swoop. Add to that the part where it isn't in the interests of the Syndicate to take such drastic action lest it be revealed to the rest of the Technocracy what they were getting up to with the SPD (which helped Pentex grow, to boot) and you have a recipe for a company that is more or less untouchable by the Syndicate without unacceptable collateral damage to the Convention itself and to the broader Western world.<br /> <br /> In a pure mage game, the Syndicate is going to be a more powerful force. In a werewolf game, Pentex will be. In a combined view, it's up for grabs, but Pentex is still a major player anyway you slice it if you involve it in a chronicle. It cannot be eradicated quickly without causing massive shocks through the economy - using magic to do it would result in another 2006 Incident and it's too big to eradicate fiscally - or implicating the Syndicate in the eyes of the other Conventions. The only way for them to approach it and not ultimately lose (even if they destroy them wholesale and it isn't noticed, the economic collapse it would create will <i>not</i> earn the Syndicate any goodwill and they're already in a bad political position within the Technocratic Union after the 2006 Incident) is to piece by piece disassemble them, and that's a game Pentex can play very well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:42:21-07:00","id":864149,"title":"","content":"Trying to destroy Pentex by tackling it company/corporation wise seems to be missing the point. The problem with Pentex and it's subsidiaries is that there are exalted Wyrm cultists directing the entire effort, tops-down, to accomplish wyrmish goals. The priority should be on killing or otherwise neutralizing them. The secondary target would be Pentex Bane &amp; Fomori production capabilities. (which aren't the same as general Pentex property, as far as I know) Pentex associated Black Spirals and other Shapechangers could also be targeted; doing so would also help flush out the Wyrm cultists, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:45:56-07:00","id":864150,"title":"","content":"Understood. Thank you very much for kind, detailed answer.<br /> <br /> Just one quick question: &quot;In a werewolf game&quot; - are you meaning backup of the BSD and other Mockery Breeds? Or you have simply meant WtA setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-12-2016, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T00:03:44-07:00","id":864154,"title":"","content":"I mean in the WtA setting when I say in a werewolf game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864149#post864149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to destroy Pentex by tackling it company/corporation wise seems to be missing the point. The problem with Pentex and it's subsidiaries is that there are exalted Wyrm cultists directing the entire effort, tops-down, to accomplish wyrmish goals. The priority should be on killing or otherwise neutralizing them. The secondary target would be Pentex Bane &amp; Fomori production capabilities. (which aren't the same as general Pentex property, as far as I know) Pentex associated Black Spirals and other Shapechangers could also be targeted; doing so would also help flush out the Wyrm cultists, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with approaching Pentex like this is that corruption (whether extreme or relatively minor) is so endemic through middle to upper management that you can't just decapitate the Board and say 'job's done, let's go home'. Any viable replacement from within the company is likely to either already be a Cultist/Fomori/Etc or to rapidly become one. You'd need to fundamentally alter the corporate culture, and the only ways to do that are either going to require the aid of the rest of the Technocracy - thus exposing the Syndicate to scrutiny for their dealings - or be slow and subtle. Unfortunately, slow and subtle is also how Pentex works. Most of their subsidiaries aren't even openly linked to the company, but are held by shell companies that own shell companies that own shell companies that comprise major shareholders of a subsidiary, and while mages should be able to get by that much easier than mortals or garou, it isn't guaranteed. This is without the argument that Pentex itself has become an incarnation of the Urge Wyrm of Greed, which would make any such effort utterly pointless as the organization <i>in and of itself</i> is thus a corruptive influence on the world.<br /> <br /> It's why Pentex makes a great adversary. You can't just chop some heads off and call it a day. You've got to confront the reality of an enemy that, at the end of the day, cannot be confronted with brute force alone, whether that force is a klaive or magic. It's the sort of enemy that takes years of hard work at the highest levels to rip out root and stem - and that's without considering the strong probability of contingency plans for if active hostilities begin, like unleashing the fomori worldwide, triggering meltdowns and oil leaks, burning down the Amazon, etc. Pentex's end-goal is to destroy the world on its own terms - if it can't set its own schedule, I don't think it'll just lie down and die. You'd have to fight it very carefully to avoid them poisoning the earth on the way out, which again makes them a great adversary.<br /> <br /> Assassin's Creed had a great line about Abstergo, and it goes for Pentex too. &quot;The average American household contains three dozen Abstergo-owned products at any given moment. If you tried to purge them from your life completely, it would be a full-time job.&quot; Just sub-in Pentex for Abstergo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T01:11:47-07:00","id":864173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=863631#post863631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What problem exactly do you suggest? Could you more elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex has a power the Syndicate does not know. It ain't love, but spirits are a real problem, if you have no concept for them. Things will just go wrong for no apparent reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11524-the_1of3","name":"The_1of3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T03:21:51-07:00","id":864194,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between people <i>in</i> an organization knowing, and the organization itself knowing. Its almost frightening how compartmentalized an organization (of any size) can be, particularly when the higher-ups don't want to deal with a particular problem at the moment. Memos get shoved to the bottom of the pile, in-person reports get disqualified (&quot;its not really that bad, is it&quot;) or rationalized away (&quot;they're just trying to get more funding&quot;) . . . If the boss doesn't want to hear it, sooner or later, you stop telling them.<br /> <br /> Which, incidentally, seems to have directly led to the revolt during World War II. The higher-ups in the Technocracy were so ecstatic that they were on the brink of total world domination, they didn't want to hear about any allegations of Nephandi corruption. It got to the point that the field agents, who were staring at the evidence every day, finally broke down and cut a deal with the Traditions to fix the problem.<br /> <br /> So there are almost certainly plenty of Technocrats who know about Pentex - its just they're not in a position to act on that knowledge. But I suspect that if you started digging through Technocratic after-action reports, you'd find a surprising number of &quot;accidental&quot; shootings of Pentex agents, &quot;collateral damage&quot; that wipes out entire Pentex facilities . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=863723#post863723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(. . .)<br /> <br /> Pentex is the ugliest side of the concept of the corporation magnified to an extreme. It doesn't just 'go away'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right - that's the whole point of Pentex. From a Mage perspective, Pentex is the Nephandic corruption of capitalism. An attempt at worldwide Descension by convincing humanity to sell its collective soul on the mass market, to give up any potential for Ascension (or self-improvement) in favor of promotions, paychecks, and low-low prices at your local superstore.<br /> <br /> After all, selling your soul one-on-one is <i>so</i> Medieval. Today's modern Nephandi has gone global, buying souls on an industrial scale, with the full backing of the worldwide financial system. Franchise opportunities coming soon! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T07:27:34-07:00","id":864280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864149#post864149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to destroy Pentex by tackling it company/corporation wise seems to be missing the point. The problem with Pentex and it's subsidiaries is that there are exalted Wyrm cultists directing the entire effort, tops-down, to accomplish wyrmish goals. The priority should be on killing or otherwise neutralizing them. The secondary target would be Pentex Bane &amp; Fomori production capabilities. (which aren't the same as general Pentex property, as far as I know) Pentex associated Black Spirals and other Shapechangers could also be targeted; doing so would also help flush out the Wyrm cultists, perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually, the vast, overwhelming majority of everyone working at every subsidiary is a completely normal human swamped in so much paperwork that they have very little free time outside of their job. Also, cultists are passe; Pentex does things as a modern business, and stripping naked to your waist to worship an evil emanation isn't one of their standard practices. It's so amateurish for these business professionals to do things that way instead of American Psycho-like. Finally, fomori are generally disposable and temporary shock troops, not the leadership, and bane production facilities went out in later 2nd edition; you won't find references to putting banes in anything in Revised or W20, which had the benefit of the power of retcon to take out that kind of blunder many years after Subsidiaries talked about how dumb putting banes in every Sunburst computer was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:01:43-07:00","id":864364,"title":"","content":"If Syndicate's magicians, agents, extraordinary operatives and private hypertech military are pitted against Pentex paramilitary, mercenary subsidiaries, BSD and Nephandi, who will ultimately prevail in the end do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-12-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:21:38-07:00","id":864382,"title":"","content":"It's an inter-game pissing match.<br /> <br /> Werewolf-oriented folks (including Mage folks that exalt the built in Triat-ish aspects) will say Pentex, because of, ya know, the Wyrm. And all.<br /> <br /> Other Mage folks will probably say the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> I'm one of the latter, but my reasoning is probably skewed to the Z-axis. Pentex depends on reality having a certain orientation and that is one that is largely built on the core areas developed and managed of the Syndicate. The Syndicate could just change the underlying economic rules that empower Pentex and leave them starved for all those resources. Particularly if they could get over their older sibling/young upstart sibling rivalry with the NWO. It wouldn't be a BANG BANG shot'em up war with a tidy beginning and end. It would be more like spending the USSR into having to reject communism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:29:33-07:00","id":864384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_1of3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864173#post864173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex has a power the Syndicate does not know. It ain't love, but spirits are a real problem, if you have no concept for them. Things will just go wrong for no apparent reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't? Syndicate members can't learn Dimensional Science? They aren't going to have their own operatives who know it ESPECIALLY because that's supposed to be a VE thing? I mean they have assembly-line hypertech production built in now with Primal Ventures, which is pretty much the raison d'etre for the It-X Time Motion Managers. Since the Syndicate absolutely 100% knows about Pentex, they haven't made sure to develop resources to counter them? <br /> <br /> They may not call them &quot;spirits&quot;, but they will know what a spirit is (EDE, PLE, whatever). They will know what a fomori is (EDE-infestation-induced-mutation&quot; (EDE-IIM? Sounds a lot like &quot;Eat 'em&quot;...) Etc. <br /> <br /> Plus they can call upon 3-4 other Conventions for assistance if they feel real specialty knowledge is needed. And they WILL help, even if Union solidarity doesn't do it for them, if the want to keep their funding...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:42:04-07:00","id":864389,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for magnificent, <i>perfect </i>answers! Opinion-wise, I'm totally in a league with you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:48:46-07:00","id":864451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864384#post864384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't?</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, I won't engage in any pissing matches here either. Do what you like in your game. Have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11524-the_1of3","name":"The_1of3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T21:36:03-07:00","id":864704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864384#post864384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Plus they can call upon 3-4 other Conventions for assistance if they feel real specialty knowledge is needed. And they WILL help, even if Union solidarity doesn't do it for them, if the want to keep their funding...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, that half of those same conventions are already looking for blood in the water with the Syndicate due to the 2006 Incident and the general overbearing nature. If the Syndicate suddenly takes action on that massive scale, their dealings with SPD WILL come out. And suddenly, you have a Technocratic civil war. When half your allies are already looking for any excuse to murder you, you don't hand them the final piece of damning evidence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864364#post864364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Syndicate's magicians, agents, extraordinary operatives and private hypertech military are pitted against Pentex paramilitary, mercenary subsidiaries, BSD and Nephandi, who will ultimately prevail in the end do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on the game and which of the two gamelines is taking the spotlight. My money would be on the Syndicate in the long run in both, but not without enormous collateral damage including a Technocratic Civil War. It depends on the rules of engagement for each side, how much collateral they're willing to cause (and it's pretty much an absolute given that Pentex's upper management is willing to cause a lot, lot more when it comes to human lives and the environment than all but the coldest Syndicate members. Only one of them is working towards the literal eradication of existence, afterall) and whether or not, in the Syndicate's case, the rest of the TU gets involved and if they can keep them from reacting with justifiable outrage and trying to destroy the Syndicate as well.<br /> <br /> It comes down again to the issue of how deeply entrenched Pentex is, assuming the WtA version is accurate for this. It can be gotten rid of, but not easily. If it came to a real fight, they'd lose - but they're going to be banking on being too big to fail in the eyes of the hypercapitalists of the Syndicate, along with their blackmail material and their ability to do enormous damage on the way down. The only 'safe' way to do it is to slowly but surely unwind them from the greater economy like a guinea worm from a foot, or to completely eradicate and replace them in a single movement. That movement might be doable for the Syndicate as a total entity working the same extended ritual at the same time, but it would almost certainly cause the sort of Paradox backlash to make the 2006 Incident seem like a minor economic hiccup, if not one that would outright eradicate the entire Convention. That's if such a thing is even possible with Pentex's spiritual backing power in play.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T01:42:12-07:00","id":864778,"title":"","content":"Loomer hits it on the nail here. Pentex in WtA is not Pentex in MtA.<br /> In one, Pentex is the big bad and is an unassailable bastion of evil that will eventually destroy Earth.<br /> In the other, Pentex is just another ominous EvilCorp and dirty laundry of the Syndicate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 04-13-2016, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:24:38-07:00","id":864839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864778#post864778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loomer hits it on the nail here. Pentex in WtA is not Pentex in MtA.<br /> In one, Pentex is the big bad and is an unassailable bastion of evil that will eventually destroy Earth.<br /> In the other, Pentex is just another ominous EvilCorp and dirty laundry of the Syndicate</div> </div> </div> </div>I have heard someone claiming VtM and WtA version of Technocracy is tremendously weaker than MtA &quot;original&quot; Technocracy. Is it ture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T05:35:00-07:00","id":864847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864839#post864839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have heard someone claiming VtM and WtA version of Technocracy is tremendously weaker than MtA &quot;original&quot; Technocracy. Is it ture?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much... if it even exists. The WoD is crossover friendly mechanically and as far as making nods and winks at each other, but the games pretty much ignore each other once the details start getting worked out. Werewolf and Mage are probably the nastiest about this. But even in Vampire, the &quot;mysterius technomages&quot; who are all presented as Hitmarks are hinted to be a part of some secret organisation. It's just that on the scale of Vampire and how much they are integrated into society, the Technocracy of Mage has to be vastly smaller and vastly less influential.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the Vampires are much less influential and everywhere in Mage then they are in Vampire.<br /> <br /> The big bad technomagical threat in Werewolf are the agents of the Weaver, and while they on the surface might look like Technocrats, they are decidedly not such. I.e. their agents are Drones, their MiB's turn into goo on death and their operatives all act in perfect unison to the The One Song of the Weaver. There are some nods to the Technocracy as a possible antagonist, but it's mostly ignored by a vast majority of Werewolf books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:28:34-07:00","id":864961,"title":"","content":"By way of example, one of the Pentex board members is Harold Zettler, a powerful vampire. Despite the fact that he is a vampire and his write up mentions a couple connections with the broader Vampire setting he really doesn't interact with the VtM game in any meaningful way. He's a Werewolf NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:43:00-07:00","id":864968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864778#post864778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loomer hits it on the nail here. Pentex in WtA is not Pentex in MtA.<br /> In one, Pentex is the big bad and is an unassailable bastion of evil that will eventually destroy Earth.<br /> In the other, Pentex is just another ominous EvilCorp and dirty laundry of the Syndicate</div> </div> </div> </div>Yanno, I don't remember encountering Pentex in MTA before WTA, but that could explain why I'm always confused why all the WTA players think Pentex is as all encompassing as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T09:08:30-07:00","id":864980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_1of3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864451#post864451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, I won't engage in any pissing matches here either. Do what you like in your game. Have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure... I guess. <br /> <br /> But, since RAW is a determinative base, just chucking an entire Sect's ability to access a full ninth of their potential power is something of a radical departure from the baseline. The Union isn't composed of mutually incompatible uber-paradigms, or even paradigms that aren't really all that compatible but with a nebulous middle ground created in the form of a lingua franca (e.g. the Traditions). The uber-paradigms interlock into an overall over-paradigm (of some sort) that is stronger and more integrated conceptually than that of the Traditions. There is no indication that Syndicate members will hear VE's talking about EDE's and go &quot;Oh, we don't believe in those,&quot; They may not know that much about them (and the ones who did, well... those guys become part of the problem), but they know the VE's know about them and dealing with them is the VE's job, not theirs (most of the time).<br /> <br /> So, if you are going to chuck that as a Golden Rule perogative, that's A-Okay, but stating it as a baseline assumption doesn't seem accurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T09:20:26-07:00","id":864987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864704#post864704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, of course, that half of those same conventions are already looking for blood in the water with the Syndicate due to the 2006 Incident and the general overbearing nature. If the Syndicate suddenly takes action on that massive scale, their dealings with SPD WILL come out. And suddenly, you have a Technocratic civil war. When half your allies are already looking for any excuse to murder you, you don't hand them the final piece of damning evidence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Largely conceded, but with the caveat that &quot;asking for help&quot; on the level to spill all those beans would mean it was an ALL-OUT-WAR scenario. Anything more subtle, like pulling out the rug by changing the rules (aka assumptions) of economics <i>just enough</i> would be possible without the inevitable reveal you're positing. And might get some traction in the form of assistance from the other Conventions if properly veiled - &quot;We're trying to make sure that nothing like 2006 CAN ever happen again&quot; (particularly if the &quot;veil&quot; is actually largely true.) <br /> <br /> In fact, I don't think the Big Reveal is a true given in the way you present, even in open warfare. Misdirection can work wonders. And the only real rivals in the Union (perhaps in the world) of the Syndicate in subtlety and guile are the NWO (who have largely been re-characterized as the Syndicates inept foils... The Syndicate as most recently presented, in many ways could almost just take over the Technocracy. They do the NWO thing better because finance is <i>obviously </i>superior to any other means of social control (sarcasm dripping). They do a lot of the It-X invention and mechanical production better than they do. That only leaves two other Conventions to integrate... and I'm sure there are Syndicate think-tanks planning out the semi-hostile takeover of enough of their inherent functions to render them redundant and just integrate the outliers. The only thing that might be keeping them from doing so might just be keeping the smoking gun of the SPD hidden. Oh, and the wishes of the Technephandi masters of the Union...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T11:54:19-07:00","id":865042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864980#post864980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They may not know that much about them (and the ones who did, well... those guys become part of the problem), but they know the VE's know about them and dealing with them is the VE's job, not theirs (most of the time).</div> </div> </div> </div>And they don't involve others in the problem. According to the RAW. The even created a pseudo-SPD so that the other conventions will not realize that anything was wrong about SPD. They even let their own pseudo-SPD agents be assassinated by Invictus just to keep that secret. Which is rather stupid, if you ask me, but hey, it's RAW. It must be true. Yeah, I might yet start to enjoy setting lawyering. It's certainly even more stupid than rules lawyering, as the rules at least aim to be consistent, while the presentation of the setting is meant to be opaque, but hey, as I said: Have fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11524-the_1of3","name":"The_1of3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T12:32:16-07:00","id":865055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The_1of3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=865042#post865042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they don't involve others in the problem. According to the RAW. The even created a pseudo-SPD so that the other conventions will not realize that anything was wrong about SPD. They even let their own pseudo-SPD agents be assassinated by Invictus just to keep that secret. Which is rather stupid, if you ask me, but hey, it's RAW. It must be true. Yeah, I might yet start to enjoy setting lawyering. It's certainly even more stupid than rules lawyering, as the rules at least aim to be consistent, while the presentation of the setting is meant to be opaque, but hey, as I said: Have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... yeah.... again.. Okay.<br /> <br /> But your premise was (is?) that the Syndicate has no knowledge of Spirit. Which was their specialty back in the ancient-most days, when the whole SPD thing was almost the umbrella concept for the Convetion. Even stepping back to a more playable direction and taking off the &quot;evil goggles&quot; and directing them first towards Entropy-ish and now to Prime-like, there is no indication that the Syndicate is Spirit-blind. That assertion doesn't seem supported by the information you've provided above or from the setting. If it's in there, I'd really like to know where as that is something to have to think around. Like the Ahl-i-Batin as Entropy-phobes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:24:01-07:00","id":865272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=864778#post864778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loomer hits it on the nail here. Pentex in WtA is not Pentex in MtA.<br /> In one, Pentex is the big bad and is an unassailable bastion of evil that will eventually destroy Earth.<br /> In the other, Pentex is just another ominous EvilCorp and dirty laundry of the Syndicate</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think its more an expression of the relative power bases. Destroying Pentex would require a war, wiping them out across all across the globe. Its not just a matter of assassinating the board - thanks to Pentex's organizational &quot;philosophy&quot; - there are countless potential successors who could replace them. To truly get rid of Pentex, you'd have to burn the company to the ground, and salt the earth<br /> <br /> And the werewolves just don't have that in them any more. They're second-tier players (at best). Oh, sure, they can hang on, lurking in the shadows of human civilization for generations - maybe even indefinitely. But they no longer have the allies, the manpower, or the resources to act on a planetary scale. And like cancer, you'd have to completely wipe out all of Pentex, or it'd just grow back. . .<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, on the other hand, is <i>also</i> a dominant world-spanning conspiracy. They've got the financial wizards to track down Pentex's hidden assets, the re-educational resources to purge the company's tainted philosophies, the cyborgs and freaky mutants to go toe-to-toe with Pentex's monstrous mercenaries. If Pentex wants a war, the Technocracy can give it to them.<br /> <br /> So its really a matter of perspectives. The Garou can't win. Sure, they're supernatural apex predators, with their own magical Gifts. But even at their height, they'd have been ill-equipped to deal with such an urban-based threat. And in the present day, such a war would be suicidal. So, <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i> describes Pentex as an unstoppable threat . . .because the Garou <i>can't</i> stop it. The Technocracy could, though - the cost-benefit analysis just isn't there yet - so Pentex is presented in <i>Mage </i>as less of a threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:03:53-07:00","id":865285,"title":"","content":"Good points. So basically Technocracy(and Mage in general) is vastly bigger and more powerful than Garou and their archenemy, Pentex, they are portrayed less a threat in the MtA?<br /> <br /> Besides, as others have elaborated, I think Syndicate alone would give them a good war and annihilate them form face of the Earth, in sphere of both military and magick. If Technocracy itself goes to open war against Pentex, that would be a pure, unadulterated stomp for Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-14-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T04:34:05-07:00","id":865417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=865272#post865272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think its more an expression of the relative power bases. Destroying Pentex would require a war, wiping them out across all across the globe. Its not just a matter of assassinating the board - thanks to Pentex's organizational &quot;philosophy&quot; - there are countless potential successors who could replace them. To truly get rid of Pentex, you'd have to burn the company to the ground, and salt the earth<br /> <br /> And the werewolves just don't have that in them any more. They're second-tier players (at best). Oh, sure, they can hang on, lurking in the shadows of human civilization for generations - maybe even indefinitely. But they no longer have the allies, the manpower, or the resources to act on a planetary scale. And like cancer, you'd have to completely wipe out all of Pentex, or it'd just grow back. . .<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, on the other hand, is <i>also</i> a dominant world-spanning conspiracy. They've got the financial wizards to track down Pentex's hidden assets, the re-educational resources to purge the company's tainted philosophies, the cyborgs and freaky mutants to go toe-to-toe with Pentex's monstrous mercenaries. If Pentex wants a war, the Technocracy can give it to them.<br /> <br /> So its really a matter of perspectives. The Garou can't win. Sure, they're supernatural apex predators, with their own magical Gifts. But even at their height, they'd have been ill-equipped to deal with such an urban-based threat. And in the present day, such a war would be suicidal. So, <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i> describes Pentex as an unstoppable threat . . .because the Garou <i>can't</i> stop it. The Technocracy could, though - the cost-benefit analysis just isn't there yet - so Pentex is presented in <i>Mage </i>as less of a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mrrrgh. I'll concede to you because this topic is in the Mage forum and that perspective is entirely valid.<br /> <br /> Syndicate is a smaller fish then Pentex in Werewolf, though. And it's not that the Garou are incapable of killing Pentex, heck there's nothing they are actually incapable of, and the point of the game is to surmount all their flaws and limitations to actually make a difference. The cost and the consequences would be staggering, but I'm pretty sure that the Garou could live with worldwide economic collapse. The fundamental problem with Pentex and Werwolf is the fact that just because you killed the bad shit, doesn't mean humans will stop doing bad shit for crap reasons. A million companies like Pentex are still out there doing the same shit and they're not even ran by monsters from beyond. Heck, 90% of all Pentex operations are completley above board, legal and ran by ordinary people.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter, because your actual problem is the fundamental human nature, and that's what you actually need to change to win. Which, ironically is a topic that even Mage could deal with - if its Pentex was anything like Werewolf's Pentex, that is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T09:59:40-07:00","id":865562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=865417#post865417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It doesn't matter, because your actual problem is the fundamental human nature, and that's what you actually need to change to win. Which, ironically is a topic that even Mage could deal with - if its Pentex was anything like Werewolf's Pentex, that is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to change &quot;fundamental human nature&quot; (whatever that actually is) to end Pentex as is, you could make a few changes in basic economics as a discipline that would move the dial away from profligate waste: Start with calculating the valuation of proximate externalities. Don't assume your resource base is inexhaustible. Etc. And you don't even have to do away with greed!<br /> <br /> And the Garou are walking furry cuisinarts with a ton of fun invisible friends, but could never really affect Pentex and it's bottom line (which would affect it's power base significantly) with anything remotely like what the Syndicate can do with promoting a couple of new books with some theories and observations already laying around. It's not like they haven't made fundamental changes to the economic model before. Hell, even before the soon-to-be High Guild joined the Order of Reason even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T14:07:30-07:00","id":865695,"title":"","content":"Why to fight when only opening the door to allow the beats entering within is enough? Because is easier to send a message to werewolves, tradional mages and another factions &quot;that it our common enemy, could you do the hard work for the good of everybody?&quot; And vampires don't allow Syndicate vs Pentex war because could break the mascarade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T05:49:46-07:00","id":1298927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/863625-technocracy-and-pentex?p=863723#post863723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic reason they don't is that Pentex is a major global actor that they can't destroy without calling <i>significant</i> attention to their own dealings - made willingly and knowingly - with a force that is, at its core, inherently opposed to the end goals of the Technocracy. They have over 134 offices worldwide, possess major market shares in pharmaceuticals, weapons manufacturing, private military companies, waste disposal, mining, energy generation, oil extraction and refining, food processing, logistics and distribution, mass market media shares, fishery operations, cosmetics, raw plastics and paper production, tobacco products, global stocks and real-estate investment, and healthcare. Through Tellus and Sunburst, they have major shares of the computing world. Nastrum brings a major market share in the aerospace and military sector. Their sticky fingers even go into education and childcare.<br /> <br /> Endron alone has seven nuclear plants in America with 5 more slated to be built as of 2000 - and if on schedule, now built and operational. They control the most important oil pipeline in the entire Middle East, the Aswan-61 pipeline. Magadon has over 60 production plants and a dozen research plants worldwide, and a <i>22.5%</i> market share in 1998. In 1999 they made 24.8 billion dollars gross, and in 2000, posted a net profit of <i>8.115 billion</i>. O'Tolley's has a 25+% market share in the CONUS - for reference, <i>McDonalds</i>, that veritable juggernaut of Greasy Meat-Based Capitalism, only has a <i>19%</i> market share IRL. In 2010, an Endron rig spilled <i>250 million gallons of oil</i> - and that barely put a dent in the company's pockets. Deepwater Horizon was 210 million.<br /> <br /> That's why the Syndicate and the Technocracy doesn't 'crush' Pentex. You don't crush Pentex without also crushing the entire Western economy with it. It isn't some pesky little tick the Technocracy can pull out - it's a tapeworm wound so deep through the entire Western economic model that if you try and brute force it out, you're going to quickly find yourself elbow-deep in blood wondering why everything is screaming. Not only would the Syndicate taking the action expose them to massive problems with the rest of the Technocracy, the Technocracy simply <i>can't</i> crush Pentex without prolonged, difficult struggle. And before anyone goes 'well they're magic!', the global financial recession happened when the Syndicate got too 'experimental' - and Pentex have their own nephandi to call on.<br /> <br /> Pentex is the ugliest side of the concept of the corporation magnified to an extreme. It doesn't just 'go away'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Necro'ing this simply because it's a really beautiful explanation of the whole Pentex/Syndicate issue, and the best one I could find online.<br /> <br /> I'd go a step further; the WoD has some huge financial players in all its settings. Pentex (basically everything, consumer-focused), Syndicate (basically everything, finance-focused), the Giovanni (oil, organized crime, politics), the Ventrue (basically everything, politics), the Grimaldi Family (the only reason the Sabbat exists, media, finances, politics). How on earth do they coexist? Why aren't they destroying eachother?<br /> <br /> Because the bottom line trumps all, and removing reality deviants / rival vampires / wyrm cultists / hereditary ghouls from your shared financial interests is just EXPENSIVE. The Syndicate could bring all its resources together to try and purge all Vampires from the world of finance but... why would they? It would mean closing some of the big fat accounts that they grow rich off of. Losing some great clients and contractors. In some cases, it could even mean losing dinner guests, and friends in high society!<br /> <br /> The financial big boys of the WoD are a mixture of deliberately ignorant and unhappy bedfellows. If you invest in a company, work for a company or own a company, you are one or two degrees of separation away from a Vampire, a Mage and a Fomorus, simply because of the nature of corporate investment*. Publicly traded companies have a huge number of investors. It's unavoidable. So all of these financial interests are like roots all tangled around eachother in the soil. The Syndicate could try and tear out another plant, but oh boy would they be hurting themselves horribly in the short term. Even if their enemies roll over and play dead, or surrender immediately, they're hurting themselves far more than they'd ever accept. THEN you can factor in vengeful Vampires/Ghouls/Spirits/Fomori/Mages/Werewolves showing up at your door asking for a &quot;private meeting&quot;.<br /> <br /> *by the same measure, IRL if you have a diverse financial portfolio (invested in several companies, hedge funds and banks) then that means you are ABSOLUTELY one or two degrees of separation from people you would despise or find objectionable, from criminals to terrorists and even politicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-23-2019, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}